-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 28: ELECTRONIC FILING SERVICE.  LAYER 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
-- Written with a macro builder that quotes the source lines and writes the @ref; the builder is not part of this row, so edit this file directly.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the Rule says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the Rule says no in its own words: a definition that says "means", a flat negative,
--                a condition introduced by "if" or "where", or a period it fixes in its own words
--                (rulings of 2026-10-29, 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05).
--   NOTHING      the Rule does not answer: it grants a power, limits its grant by its own wording, is
--                silent, or points outside the sources.  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer: every requirement in these Rules is subject to the Court's
-- discretion to order otherwise in the interests of justice.  It is not threaded through the functions.
--
-- "DEEMED" in this Order means "deemed until the contrary is proved" (r 1).  Every deeming function
-- below therefore takes `the contrary is proved` and answers through the helper
-- `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands`.
--
-- SEAMS this module answers for other parts: S-F1 `o 28 r 10 the moment the document is deemed filed`,
-- S-F2 `o 28 r 11 the moment time for service begins to run`, S-S2 `o 28 r 12 the moment service is deemed effected`.
-- SEAMS it takes as inputs: `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` (every period), `o 7 r 8 the day service is deemed effected`.

