    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“electronic transmission” means electronic transmission by an authorised user or a registered user through the electronic filing service"

-- “entity” means a sole proprietorship, an incorporated or unincorporated partnership (including a
-- limited liability partnership and a limited partnership), a law corporation, a company or other body
-- corporate, the Attorney-General's Chambers, a department of the Government or a public authority.
DECLARE `o 28 r 1 kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `o 28 r 1 sole proprietorship`
    `o 28 r 1 incorporated or unincorporated partnership (including a limited liability partnership and a limited partnership)`
    `o 28 r 1 law corporation`
    `o 28 r 1 company or other body corporate`
    `o 28 r 1 the Attorney-General's Chambers`
    `o 28 r 1 department of the Government`
    `o 28 r 1 public authority`
    `o 28 r 1 any other kind of body`

-- src:4202 | “entity” means a sole proprietorship, an incorporated or unincorporated partnership (including a limited liability partnership and a limited partnership), a law corporation, a company or other body corporate, the Attorney‑General’s Chambers, a department of the Government or a public authority;
@ref O 28 r 1 “entity” (src:4202)
GIVEN body IS A `o 28 r 1 kind of body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 1 a body is an entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `o 28 r 1 any other kind of body` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“entity” means a sole proprietorship, an incorporated or unincorporated partnership (including a limited liability partnership and a limited partnership), a law corporation, a company or other body corporate, the Attorney‑General’s Chambers, a department of the Government or a public authority"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

