-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 7 -- the fee for a registered user`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- r 7(1): the fee is payable by each registered user "other than a service bureau".  The parenthesis takes
-- a service bureau out of what the grant of a charge covers: NOTHING for a service bureau (QE default).
-- src:4229 | 7. —(1) Subject to paragraphs (2) and (3), the following fee is payable by each registered user, other than a service bureau: ( a )
@ref O 28 r 7(1) the fee is payable (src:4229)
GIVEN `the registered user is a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(1) the fee is payable by the registered user` MEANS
    IF NOT `the registered user is a service bureau`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the following fee is payable by each registered user, other than a service bureau" (open convention question QE)

-- r 7(1)(a) to (h): the monthly fee, by the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time.
-- Paragraph (2) says whom to count in some contexts: see `o 28 r 7(2) the number counted in place of advocates and solicitors`.
-- A count of nought is in no band: NOTHING.
-- src:4229 | 7. —(1) Subject to paragraphs (2) and (3), the following fee is payable by each registered user, other than a service bureau: ( a )
-- src:4230 | where the registered user is an entity comprising a single advocate and solicitor as at the relevant time in a year, $25 per month or part of a month;
-- src:4231 | ( b )
