GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 28 r 7(1) the monthly fee for a registered user` MEANS
    --                                                           dollars per month or part of a month
    BRANCH IF `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` EQUALS 1          THEN JUST 25      -- (a) a single advocate and solicitor
           IF `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT LEAST 2   AND `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT MOST 5   THEN JUST 35     -- (b) 2 to 5
           IF `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT LEAST 6   AND `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT MOST 9   THEN JUST 70     -- (c) 6 to 9
           IF `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT LEAST 10  AND `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT MOST 19  THEN JUST 140    -- (d) 10 to 19
           IF `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT LEAST 20  AND `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT MOST 49  THEN JUST 250    -- (e) 20 to 49
           IF `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT LEAST 50  AND `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT MOST 99  THEN JUST 500    -- (f) 50 to 99
           IF `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT LEAST 100 AND `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT MOST 199 THEN JUST 1000   -- (g) 100 to 199
           IF `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` AT LEAST 200 THEN JUST 2000                                                                   -- (h) 200 or more
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no band of paragraph (1) describes this number

-- The fee "per month or part of a month": the number of months charged counts a part of a month as a month.
@ref O 28 r 7(1) per month or part of a month (src:4229-4244)
GIVEN `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months or parts of a month charged` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 28 r 7(1) the fee for a number of months or parts of a month` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 28 r 7(1) the monthly fee for a registered user` `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time`
    WHEN JUST monthly THEN JUST (monthly TIMES `the number of months or parts of a month charged`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no band of paragraph (1) describes this number

-- r 7(2): who is counted as an "advocate and solicitor".
DECLARE `o 28 r 7(2) kind of registered user` IS ONE OF
    `o 28 r 7(2)(a) the Attorney-General's Chambers`
    `o 28 r 7(2)(b) a department of the Government or a public authority`
    `o 28 r 7(2)(c) an entity registered solely to search or inspect under Order 26, Rule 3`
    `o 28 r 7(2)(d) an entity comprising registered foreign lawyers and no advocate and solicitor`
    `o 28 r 7(2)(e) an entity comprising advocates and solicitors and registered foreign lawyers`
    `o 28 r 7(2) any other registered user`

-- The heads that could be counted, as the registered user can state them.
DECLARE `o 28 r 7(2) headcounts` HAS
    `o 28 r 7(2) advocates and solicitors` IS A NUMBER
    `o 28 r 7(2)(a) the Attorney-General, a Deputy Attorney-General, the Solicitor-General or a State Counsel or Deputy Public Prosecutor` IS A NUMBER
    `o 28 r 7(2)(b) persons employed or engaged by the registered user who have a right to appear before the court by virtue of a written law` IS A NUMBER
    `o 28 r 7(2)(c) authorised users designated by the registered user` IS A NUMBER
    `o 28 r 7(2)(d) registered foreign lawyers` IS A NUMBER

-- src:4245 | (2) Paragraph (1) applies in the following contexts with the following modifications: ( a )
-- src:4246 | where the registered user is the Attorney‑General’s Chambers, a reference to an advocate and solicitor is read as a reference to a person who is the Attorney‑General, a Deputy Attorney‑General, the Solicitor‑General or a State Counsel or Deputy Public Prosecutor;
-- src:4247 | ( b )
-- src:4248 | where the registered user is a department of the Government or a public authority, a reference to an advocate and solicitor is read as a reference to a person who — (i)
-- src:4249 | is employed or engaged by the registered user; and
-- src:4250 | (ii)
-- src:4251 | has a right to appear before the court by virtue of any written law;
-- src:4252 | ( c )
-- src:4253 | where the registered user is an entity that is registered solely for the purpose of using the electronic filing service to search the information referred to in Order 26, Rule 3(1), or to search for, inspect or take a copy of any document filed in the Registry, in accordance with Order 26, Rule 3(4), (8), (9) and (10), a reference to an advocate and solicitor is read as a reference to an authorised user designated by the registered user;
-- src:4254 | ( d )
-- src:4255 | subject to sub‑paragraph ( e ), where the registered user is an entity comprising one or more registered foreign lawyers, a reference to an advocate and solicitor is read as a reference to a registered foreign lawyer;
-- src:4256 | ( e )
-- src:4257 | where the registered user is an entity comprising one or more advocates and solicitors and one or more registered foreign lawyers, a reference to an advocate and solicitor is read as a reference to an advocate and solicitor or a registered foreign lawyer.
@ref O 28 r 7(2) (src:4245-4257)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 28 r 7(2) kind of registered user`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(2) paragraph (1) applies with a modification` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(2) any other registered user` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) applies in the following contexts with the following modifications: where the registered user is ..." (no listed context holds)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref O 28 r 7(2) (src:4245-4257)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 28 r 7(2) kind of registered user`
      heads IS A `o 28 r 7(2) headcounts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 28 r 7(2) the number counted in place of advocates and solicitors` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(2)(a) the Attorney-General's Chambers` THEN heads's `o 28 r 7(2)(a) the Attorney-General, a Deputy Attorney-General, the Solicitor-General or a State Counsel or Deputy Public Prosecutor`
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(2)(b) a department of the Government or a public authority` THEN heads's `o 28 r 7(2)(b) persons employed or engaged by the registered user who have a right to appear before the court by virtue of a written law`
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(2)(c) an entity registered solely to search or inspect under Order 26, Rule 3` THEN heads's `o 28 r 7(2)(c) authorised users designated by the registered user`
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(2)(d) an entity comprising registered foreign lawyers and no advocate and solicitor` THEN heads's `o 28 r 7(2)(d) registered foreign lawyers`
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(2)(e) an entity comprising advocates and solicitors and registered foreign lawyers` THEN heads's `o 28 r 7(2) advocates and solicitors` PLUS heads's `o 28 r 7(2)(d) registered foreign lawyers`
    OTHERWISE heads's `o 28 r 7(2) advocates and solicitors`

-- r 7(3): no fee for an entity registered solely to make the two kinds of application.
-- src:4258 | (3) Where the registered user is an entity that is registered solely for the purpose of using the electronic filing service to make one or more of the following applications under the Legal Profession Act 1966, no fee is payable by the registered user: ( a )
-- src:4259 | an application under section 18(2) of that Act for a provisional practising certificate;
-- src:4260 | ( b )
-- src:4261 | an application under section 25(1) of that Act for a practising certificate. [S 310/2025 wef 26/05/2025]
@ref O 28 r 7(3) (src:4258-4261)
GIVEN `the registered user is an entity registered solely for the purpose of using the electronic filing service to make applications under the Legal Profession Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each application is under section 18(2) of that Act for a provisional practising certificate or under section 25(1) for a practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(3) no fee is payable by the registered user` MEANS
    IF `the registered user is an entity registered solely for the purpose of using the electronic filing service to make applications under the Legal Profession Act 1966` AND `each application is under section 18(2) of that Act for a provisional practising certificate or under section 25(1) for a practising certificate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the registered user is an entity that is registered solely for the purpose of using the electronic filing service to make one or more of the following applications under the Legal Profession Act 1966, no fee is payable by the registered user"

-- r 7(4): the "relevant time".
DECLARE `o 28 r 7(4) how a relevant time arises` IS ONE OF
    `o 28 r 7(4)(a) 1 May in any year`
    `o 28 r 7(4)(b) the entity registers for the first time under Rule 6`
    `o 28 r 7(4)(c) the entity is deemed registered before 1 April 2022`
    `o 28 r 7(4)(d) the registered user informs the Registrar after 1 May of a change in the number of advocates and solicitors`

-- src:4262 | (4) In paragraph (1), “relevant time” means — ( a )
-- src:4263 | 1 May in any year unless sub‑paragraphs ( b ) and ( c ) apply;
-- src:4264 | ( b )
-- src:4265 | where an entity registers for the first time under Rule 6 — the date of first registration;
-- src:4266 | ( c )
-- src:4267 | where an entity is deemed to have been registered as a registered user before 1 April 2022 — 1 April 2022; and
-- src:4268 | ( d )
-- src:4269 | where a registered user informs the Registrar after 1 May in any year of any change in the number of its advocates and solicitors — the day on which the Registrar is so informed.
@ref O 28 r 7(4) relevant time (src:4262-4269)
GIVEN how IS A `o 28 r 7(4) how a relevant time arises`
      year IS A NUMBER
      `the date of first registration` IS A DATE
      `the day the Registrar is informed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 28 r 7(4) the relevant time` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(4)(a) 1 May in any year` THEN JUST (Date 1 5 year)
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(4)(b) the entity registers for the first time under Rule 6` THEN JUST `the date of first registration`
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(4)(c) the entity is deemed registered before 1 April 2022` THEN JUST (Date 1 4 2022)
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(4)(d) the registered user informs the Registrar after 1 May of a change in the number of advocates and solicitors` THEN
        IF `the day the Registrar is informed` GREATER THAN (Date 1 5 year)
        THEN JUST `the day the Registrar is informed`
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "informs the Registrar after 1 May in any year"

-- The yes/no twin of the date above (a date cannot carry JUST FALSE): does this way of arising give a relevant time?
-- Sub-paragraph (a) reads "unless sub-paragraphs (b) and (c) apply" as "unless (b) or (c) applies" (fork F-28-1).
@ref O 28 r 7(4) relevant time (src:4262-4269)
GIVEN how IS A `o 28 r 7(4) how a relevant time arises`
      `the entity registers for the first time under Rule 6 in the year asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is deemed registered before 1 April 2022` IS A BOOLEAN
      year IS A NUMBER
      `the day the Registrar is informed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(4) a relevant time arises in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(4)(a) 1 May in any year` THEN
        IF `the entity registers for the first time under Rule 6 in the year asked about` OR `the entity is deemed registered before 1 April 2022`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "1 May in any year unless sub‑paragraphs ( b ) and ( c ) apply"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(4)(b) the entity registers for the first time under Rule 6` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(4)(c) the entity is deemed registered before 1 April 2022` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 28 r 7(4)(d) the registered user informs the Registrar after 1 May of a change in the number of advocates and solicitors` THEN
        IF `the day the Registrar is informed` GREATER THAN (Date 1 5 year)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a registered user informs the Registrar after 1 May in any year"

-- r 7(5): the fee starts to be payable from, and in respect of, the first month in which the relevant time falls.
-- src:4270 | (5) The fee mentioned in paragraph (1) starts to be payable from and in respect of the first month in which the relevant time falls, and continues to be payable monthly.
@ref O 28 r 7(5) (src:4270)
GIVEN `the relevant time` IS A DATE
      `a day in the month asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(5) the fee is payable for the month` MEANS
    IF ((DATE_YEAR `a day in the month asked about`) TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `a day in the month asked about`) AT LEAST ((DATE_YEAR `the relevant time`) TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the relevant time`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "starts to be payable from and in respect of the first month in which the relevant time falls"

-- r 7(6): due and payable on the first day of each month.
-- src:4271 | (6) The fee payable by each registered user is due and payable on the first day of each month.
@ref O 28 r 7(6) (src:4271)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`o 28 r 7(6) the day the fee for a month is due and payable` MEANS Date 1 month year

@ref O 28 r 7(6) (src:4271)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      year IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(6) the fee for the month is due and payable on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day` EQUALS `o 28 r 7(6) the day the fee for a month is due and payable` year month
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is due and payable on the first day of each month"

-- src:4272 | (7) The Registrar may waive, refund or defer the payment of the whole or any part of the fee in paragraph (1) in relation to any registered user or class of registered users on such terms and conditions as the Registrar deems fit.
@ref O 28 r 7(7) (src:4272)
GIVEN `the waiver, refund or deferment is in relation to a registered user or class of registered users` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is on terms and conditions the Registrar deems fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(7) the Registrar may waive, refund or defer the fee` MEANS
    IF `the waiver, refund or deferment is in relation to a registered user or class of registered users` AND `it is on terms and conditions the Registrar deems fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may waive, refund or defer the payment of the whole or any part of the fee in paragraph (1) in relation to any registered user or class of registered users on such terms and conditions as the Registrar deems fit"

-- r 7(8)(a): the Registrar MUST refund an amount paid in excess or error if the claim in writing is made within
-- 3 months after the date of payment.  The period gives out in its own words: after it, JUST FALSE for this duty.
-- src:4273 | (8) Where any fee under this Rule has been paid in excess or error by a registered user, the Registrar — ( a )
-- src:4274 | must refund the amount paid in excess or error if the registered user makes a claim in writing to the Registrar within 3 months after the date on which the fee was paid in excess or error; and
@ref O 28 r 7(8)(a) (src:4273-4274)
GIVEN `the amount was paid in excess or error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim was made in writing to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim was made within the 3 months` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(8)(a) the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error (the duty arises)` MEANS
    IF `the amount was paid in excess or error` AND `the claim was made in writing to the Registrar`
    THEN `the claim was made within the 3 months`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the registered user makes a claim in writing to the Registrar within 3 months after the date on which the fee was paid in excess or error"

@ref O 28 r 7(8)(a) compliance (src:4273-4274)
GIVEN `the amount was paid in excess or error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim was made in writing to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim was made within the 3 months` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has refunded the amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(8)(a) the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error` MEANS
    IF `o 28 r 7(8)(a) the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error (the duty arises)` `the amount was paid in excess or error` `the claim was made in writing to the Registrar` `the claim was made within the 3 months` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the Registrar has refunded the amount`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): a bare "must refund": not yet done (open convention question QB)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the trigger is unmet or undecided, so the duty does not arise; `o 28 r 7(8)(a) the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error (the duty arises)` says so (open convention question QD)

-- The helper every period function in this module calls.  It is named for the first rule that needs it, r 7(8)(a),
-- and is used by every later rule that fixes a period in its own words.
--   done    the date the act was done, or NOTHING if it has not been done
--   `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`   the last day, counted under Order 3, Rule 3 (an input: that rule is in another part)
--   `the date asked about`   the date as at which the question is put
-- Done on or before the last day: JUST TRUE.  Done after it: JUST FALSE.  Not done, and the last day has not passed: NOTHING
-- (the period is still running and the text says nothing yet).  Not done, and the last day has passed: JUST FALSE.
@ref O 28 r 7(8)(a) within 3 months (src:4273-4274)
GIVEN done IS A MAYBE DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(8)(a) the act is done by the last day` MEANS
    CONSIDER done
    WHEN JUST day THEN
        IF day AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the text fixes the period in its own words, and the act was done after its last day
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date asked about` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period is still running and the act is not yet done
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the text fixes the period in its own words, and it ended without the act

-- src:4273 | (8) Where any fee under this Rule has been paid in excess or error by a registered user, the Registrar — ( a )
-- src:4274 | must refund the amount paid in excess or error if the registered user makes a claim in writing to the Registrar within 3 months after the date on which the fee was paid in excess or error; and
@ref O 28 r 7(8)(a) claim (src:4273-4274)
`o 28 r 7(8)(a) the period for the claim` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 3
    `period unit` IS Months
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`
@ref O 28 r 7(8)(a) claim (src:4273-4274)
GIVEN done IS A MAYBE DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(8)(a) the claim is made in writing in time` MEANS
    `o 28 r 7(8)(a) the act is done by the last day` done `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `the date asked about`  -- period in its own words: "within 3 months after the date on which the fee was paid in excess or error"

-- src:4275 | ( b )
-- src:4276 | may, in any other case, as the Registrar deems fit, refund the whole or any part of the amount paid in excess or error.
@ref O 28 r 7(8)(b) (src:4275-4276)
GIVEN `the amount was paid in excess or error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is not one in which paragraph (a) requires a refund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(8)(b) the Registrar may refund in any other case` MEANS
    IF `the amount was paid in excess or error` AND `the case is not one in which paragraph (a) requires a refund`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, in any other case, as the Registrar deems fit, refund the whole or any part of the amount paid in excess or error"
-- src:4277 | (9) For the purposes of this Rule, the manner in which the entity is to inform the Registrar of the number of advocates and solicitors and all matters connected with or incidental to this subject may be set out in any practice directions for the time being issued by the Registrar.
@ref O 28 r 7(9) (src:4277)
GIVEN `a practice direction issued by the Registrar sets out the manner in which the entity is to inform the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 7(9) the manner of informing the Registrar is set out in practice directions` MEANS
    IF `a practice direction issued by the Registrar sets out the manner in which the entity is to inform the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the manner in which the entity is to inform the Registrar of the number of advocates and solicitors and all matters connected with or incidental to this subject may be set out in any practice directions for the time being issued by the Registrar"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 8 -- electronic filing`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- r 8(1): the companion that says whether the requirement arises, then the compliance function (QD).
-- src:4279 | 8. —(1) Where a document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under any other provision of these Rules, it must be so filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service in accordance with this Order and any practice directions for the time being issued by the Registrar. (2) For the purpose of paragraph (1), any requirement for the filing, service, delivery or otherwise conveyance of a document is satisfied by the filing, service, delivery or otherwise conveyance of a single copy using the electronic filing service in accordance with this Order.
@ref O 28 r 8(1) arises (src:4279)
GIVEN `the document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under another provision of these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(1) the requirement to use the electronic filing service arises` MEANS
    IF `the document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under another provision of these Rules`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under any other provision of these Rules"
-- src:4279 | 8. —(1) Where a document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under any other provision of these Rules, it must be so filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service in accordance with this Order and any practice directions for the time being issued by the Registrar. (2) For the purpose of paragraph (1), any requirement for the filing, service, delivery or otherwise conveyance of a document is satisfied by the filing, service, delivery or otherwise conveyance of a single copy using the electronic filing service in accordance with this Order.
@ref O 28 r 8(1) (src:4279)
GIVEN `the document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under another provision of these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is so conveyed using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done in accordance with this Order and the practice directions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(1) the document is filed using the electronic filing service as required` MEANS
    IF `the document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under another provision of these Rules` AND `it is so conveyed using the electronic filing service` AND `it is done in accordance with this Order and the practice directions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "it must be so filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service in accordance with this Order and any practice directions" (a bare must not done; open convention question QB)
-- src:4279 | 8. —(1) Where a document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under any other provision of these Rules, it must be so filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service in accordance with this Order and any practice directions for the time being issued by the Registrar. (2) For the purpose of paragraph (1), any requirement for the filing, service, delivery or otherwise conveyance of a document is satisfied by the filing, service, delivery or otherwise conveyance of a single copy using the electronic filing service in accordance with this Order.
@ref O 28 r 8(2) (src:4279)
GIVEN `a single copy is filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in accordance with this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(2) the requirement is satisfied by a single copy filed using the electronic filing service` MEANS
    IF `a single copy is filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service` AND `it is in accordance with this Order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any requirement for the filing, service, delivery or otherwise conveyance of a document is satisfied by the filing, service, delivery or otherwise conveyance of a single copy using the electronic filing service in accordance with this Order"

-- r 8(3): "may be done in one of 2 ways": by electronic transmission or via a service bureau.
-- src:4280 | (3) Filing, service, delivery or conveyance of a document using the electronic filing service pursuant to paragraph (1) may be done in one of 2 ways — ( a )
-- src:4281 | by electronic transmission; or
-- src:4282 | ( b )
-- src:4283 | via a service bureau.
@ref O 28 r 8(3) (src:4280-4283)
GIVEN `it is done by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done via a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(3) the way of using the electronic filing service is one of the 2 ways` MEANS
    IF `it is done by electronic transmission` OR `it is done via a service bureau`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be done in one of 2 ways — by electronic transmission; or via a service bureau"

-- src:4284 | (4) Despite anything in paragraph (1), the Registrar may allow a document, part of a document or any class of documents to be filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed other than by using the electronic filing service.
@ref O 28 r 8(4) (src:4284)
GIVEN `the Registrar has allowed the document, part of a document or class of documents to be so conveyed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(4) a document may be filed other than using the electronic filing service` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has allowed the document, part of a document or class of documents to be so conveyed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite anything in paragraph (1), the Registrar may allow a document, part of a document or any class of documents to be filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed other than by using the electronic filing service"

-- r 8(5): the form of the document.  (a) practice directions; (b) remotely composed, the form made available through the
-- service; failing any prescription, the form of Order 3, Rule 6.  A bare "must" (QB): not met is NOTHING.
-- src:4285 | (5) The form of any document must be as set out — ( a )
-- src:4286 | in any practice directions for the time being issued by the Registrar; or
-- src:4287 | ( b )
-- src:4288 | where the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider, in the form made available through the electronic filing service,
-- src:4289 | and must, in the absence of such prescription, be in the form prescribed by Order 3, Rule 6.
@ref O 28 r 8(5) (src:4285-4289)
GIVEN `the document is in the form set out in the practice directions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is remotely composed on the provider's computer system and is in the form made available through the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no such prescription and the document is in the form prescribed by Order 3, Rule 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(5) the form of the document is as required` MEANS
    IF `the document is in the form set out in the practice directions` OR `the document is remotely composed on the provider's computer system and is in the form made available through the service` OR `there is no such prescription and the document is in the form prescribed by Order 3, Rule 6`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "The form of any document must be as set out" (a bare must not done; open convention question QB)

-- src:4290 | (6) Any document which is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service by a registered user using an identification code is deemed to have been so filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by the registered user and with the registered user’s intention to do so.
@ref O 28 r 8(6) (src:4290)
GIVEN `the document is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is by a registered user` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(6) the document is deemed filed by the registered user with that user's intention` MEANS
    IF `the document is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` AND `it is by a registered user` AND `it is done using an identification code`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is deemed to have been so filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by the registered user and with the registered user’s intention to do so"
-- src:4291 | (7) Any document which is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service by an authorised user (other than an employee of a service bureau) using an identification code is deemed to have been so filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed — ( a )
-- src:4292 | by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the registered user to whom the authorised user belongs; and
@ref O 28 r 8(7)(a) (src:4291-4292)
GIVEN `the document is conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is by an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(7)(a) the document is deemed conveyed by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the registered user` MEANS
    IF `the document is conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` AND `it is by an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau` AND `it is done using an identification code`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the registered user to whom the authorised user belongs" (open convention question QE)
-- src:4293 | ( b )
-- src:4294 | with the intention of that registered user to do so.
@ref O 28 r 8(7)(b) (src:4293-4294)
GIVEN `the document is conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is by an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(7)(b) the document is deemed conveyed with the intention of the registered user` MEANS
    IF `the document is conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` AND `it is by an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau` AND `it is done using an identification code`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the intention of that registered user to do so" (open convention question QE)
-- src:4295 | (8) Any document which is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service by an authorised user, who is an employee of a service bureau, using an identification code is deemed to have been so filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed — ( a )
-- src:4296 | on behalf and with the authority of the person tendering the document to the service bureau for such purpose and with the intention of that person to do so; or
@ref O 28 r 8(8)(a) (src:4295-4296)
GIVEN `the document is conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is by an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(8)(a) the document is deemed conveyed on behalf and with the authority of the person tendering it` MEANS
    IF `the document is conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` AND `it is by an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau` AND `it is done using an identification code`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on behalf and with the authority of the person tendering the document to the service bureau for such purpose and with the intention of that person to do so"
-- src:4297 | ( b )
-- src:4298 | where the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for his or her principal, on behalf and with the authority of his or her principal and with the intention of the principal to do so.
@ref O 28 r 8(8)(b) (src:4297-4298)
GIVEN `the document is conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is by an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for a principal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(8)(b) the document is deemed conveyed on behalf and with the authority of the principal` MEANS
    IF `the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for a principal`
    THEN IF `the document is conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` AND `it is by an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau` AND `it is done using an identification code`
         THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for his or her principal, on behalf and with the authority of his or her principal and with the intention of the principal to do so"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for his or her principal, on behalf and with the authority of his or her principal and with the intention of the principal to do so"
-- src:4299 | (9) To avoid doubt, it is declared that a document which is filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar using an identification code in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service is a secure electronic record within the meaning of the Electronic Transactions Act.
@ref O 28 r 8(9) (src:4299)
GIVEN `the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed to the Registrar using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 8(9) the document is a secure electronic record` MEANS
    IF `the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed to the Registrar using an identification code` AND `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "a document which is filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar using an identification code in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service is a secure electronic record within the meaning of the Electronic Transactions Act"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 9 -- signing of electronic documents`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4301 | 9. —(1) Where a document is filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service, any requirement under these Rules relating to signing by or the signature of an authorised user or a registered user, is deemed to be complied with if the identification code of the authorised user or registered user has been applied to or associated with, directly or indirectly, the document or the transmission containing the document. (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1) — ( a )
@ref O 28 r 9(1) (src:4301)
GIVEN `the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the identification code of the authorised user or registered user has been applied to or associated with the document or the transmission containing it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 9(1) a requirement of signing by an authorised user or a registered user is deemed complied with` MEANS
    IF `the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed using the electronic filing service` AND `the identification code of the authorised user or registered user has been applied to or associated with the document or the transmission containing it`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any requirement under these Rules relating to signing by or the signature of an authorised user or a registered user, is deemed to be complied with if the identification code of the authorised user or registered user has been applied to or associated with, directly or indirectly, the document or the transmission containing the document"
-- src:4302 | where the identification code of a registered user is applied to or associated with, directly or indirectly, a document or a transmission containing a document in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service — (i)
-- src:4303 | the document is deemed to be signed by the registered user; and
@ref O 28 r 9(2)(a)(i) (src:4302-4303)
GIVEN `the registered user's identification code is applied to or associated with the document or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 9(2)(a)(i) the document is deemed signed by the registered user` MEANS
    IF `the registered user's identification code is applied to or associated with the document or transmission` AND `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the document is deemed to be signed by the registered user"
-- src:4304 | (ii)
-- src:4305 | the contents of the document are deemed to be endorsed by the registered user;
@ref O 28 r 9(2)(a)(ii) (src:4304-4305)
GIVEN `the registered user's identification code is applied to or associated with the document or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 9(2)(a)(ii) the contents are deemed endorsed by the registered user` MEANS
    IF `the registered user's identification code is applied to or associated with the document or transmission` AND `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the contents of the document are deemed to be endorsed by the registered user"
-- src:4307 | where the identification code of an authorised user (other than an employee of a service bureau) is applied to or associated with, directly or indirectly, a document or a transmission containing a document in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service — (i)
-- src:4308 | the document is deemed to be signed by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the registered user to whom the authorised user belongs; and
