      `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 9(2)(b)(i) the document is deemed signed by the authorised user on behalf of the registered user` MEANS
    IF `the identification code of an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau is applied to or associated with the document or transmission` AND `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the document is deemed to be signed by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the registered user to whom the authorised user belongs" (open convention question QE)
-- src:4309 | (ii)
-- src:4310 | the contents of the document are deemed to be endorsed by that registered user; or
@ref O 28 r 9(2)(b)(ii) (src:4309-4310)
