      `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 9(2)(b)(ii) the contents are deemed endorsed by the registered user` MEANS
    IF `the identification code of an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau is applied to or associated with the document or transmission` AND `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the contents of the document are deemed to be endorsed by that registered user" (open convention question QE)
-- src:4312 | where the identification code of an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau, is applied to or associated with, directly or indirectly, a document or a transmission containing a document in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service — (i)
-- src:4313 | the document is deemed to be signed by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the person tendering the document to the service bureau and the contents of the document are deemed to be endorsed by that person; or
@ref O 28 r 9(2)(c)(i) (src:4312-4313)
GIVEN `the identification code of an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau is applied to or associated with the document or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 9(2)(c)(i) the document is deemed signed on behalf of the person tendering it` MEANS
    IF `the identification code of an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau is applied to or associated with the document or transmission` AND `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the document is deemed to be signed by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the person tendering the document to the service bureau and the contents of the document are deemed to be endorsed by that person"
-- src:4314 | (ii)
-- src:4315 | where the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for his or her principal, the document is deemed to be signed on behalf and with the authority of his or her principal and the contents of the document are deemed to be endorsed by his or her principal.
@ref O 28 r 9(2)(c)(ii) (src:4314-4315)
GIVEN `the identification code of an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau is applied to or associated with the document or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for a principal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 9(2)(c)(ii) the document is deemed signed on behalf of the principal` MEANS
    IF `the identification code of an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau is applied to or associated with the document or transmission` AND `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` AND `the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for a principal`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for his or her principal, the document is deemed to be signed on behalf and with the authority of his or her principal"
-- src:4316 | (3) Where any written law or practice direction requires the signature of an advocate or solicitor, such requirement is deemed to be met where the identification code of the advocate or solicitor has been applied to or associated with, directly or indirectly, the document or the transmission containing the document to be signed in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service.
@ref O 28 r 9(3) (src:4316)
GIVEN `a written law or practice direction requires the signature of an advocate or solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the identification code of the advocate or solicitor has been applied to or associated with the document or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 9(3) the requirement for the signature of an advocate or solicitor is deemed met` MEANS
    IF `a written law or practice direction requires the signature of an advocate or solicitor` AND `the identification code of the advocate or solicitor has been applied to or associated with the document or transmission` AND `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such requirement is deemed to be met where the identification code of the advocate or solicitor has been applied to or associated with, directly or indirectly, the document or the transmission containing the document to be signed in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service"
-- src:4317 | (4) To avoid doubt, it is declared that the application to or association of the identification code of an authorised user or a registered user, directly or indirectly, with a document or a transmission containing a document in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service is a secure electronic signature within the meaning of the Electronic Transactions Act.
@ref O 28 r 9(4) (src:4317)
GIVEN `the identification code of an authorised user or a registered user is applied to or associated with a document or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 9(4) the application of the identification code is a secure electronic signature` MEANS
    IF `the identification code of an authorised user or a registered user is applied to or associated with a document or transmission` AND `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "is a secure electronic signature within the meaning of the Electronic Transactions Act"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 10 -- the date of filing (seam S-F1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 28 r 10(1) how the document reached the Registrar` IS ONE OF
    `o 28 r 10(1)(a) by electronic transmission from the computer system of the authorised user or registered user`
    `o 28 r 10(1)(b) remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider`
    `o 28 r 10(1)(c) via a service bureau`

-- The deeming of r 10(1): the twin that carries JUST FALSE (the moment, below, is a Moment and cannot).
-- src:4319 | 10. —(1) Where a document is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service and is subsequently accepted by the Registrar, it is deemed to be filed, served, delivered or conveyed — ( a )
-- src:4320 | where the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed by electronic transmission from the computer system of the authorised user or registered user, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider in the computer system of the electronic filing service provider;
-- src:4321 | ( b )
-- src:4322 | where the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider in the computer system of the electronic filing service provider; and
-- src:4323 | ( c )
-- src:4324 | where the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed via a service bureau, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the Registrar in the computer system of the Registrar.
@ref O 28 r 10(1) (src:4319-4324)
GIVEN `the document is filed with, served on, delivered or conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is subsequently accepted by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 10(1) the document is deemed filed, served, delivered or conveyed` MEANS
    IF `the document is filed with, served on, delivered or conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service` AND `the document is subsequently accepted by the Registrar`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a document is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service and is subsequently accepted by the Registrar, it is deemed to be filed"

-- r 10(2): the two caveats are taken out of paragraph (1): a flat negative.
-- src:4325 | (2) Paragraph (1) does not apply to the following documents: ( a )
-- src:4326 | a caveat against the issue of a warrant to arrest the property filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 5;
-- src:4327 | ( b )
-- src:4328 | a caveat against the issue of a release and payment out of Court filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 14.
@ref O 28 r 10(2) (src:4325-4328)
GIVEN `the document is a caveat against the issue of a warrant to arrest filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a caveat against release and payment out of Court filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 14` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 10(2) paragraph (1) applies to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is a caveat against the issue of a warrant to arrest filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 5` OR `the document is a caveat against release and payment out of Court filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 14`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply to the following documents"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) speaks only of the two caveats

-- The moment (S-F1).  The result is the moment the document is DEEMED filed; it means something only where the twin
-- `o 28 r 10(1) the document is deemed filed, served, delivered or conveyed` (or r 10(3) for a caveat) is JUST TRUE.
--   ordinary document   (1)(a) and (b): the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved in the PROVIDER's system;
--                       (1)(c) via a service bureau: the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved in the REGISTRAR's system.
--   caveat of r 10(2)   (3)(a) and (b): the moment the Registrar accepts it, as reflected in the Registrar's system.
--   r 10(6)             an earlier moment the Registrar has caused the service to reflect displaces all of those.
-- src:4319 | 10. —(1) Where a document is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service and is subsequently accepted by the Registrar, it is deemed to be filed, served, delivered or conveyed — ( a )
-- src:4320 | where the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed by electronic transmission from the computer system of the authorised user or registered user, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider in the computer system of the electronic filing service provider;
-- src:4321 | ( b )
-- src:4322 | where the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider in the computer system of the electronic filing service provider; and
-- src:4323 | ( c )
-- src:4324 | where the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed via a service bureau, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the Registrar in the computer system of the Registrar.
-- src:4325 | (2) Paragraph (1) does not apply to the following documents: ( a )
-- src:4326 | a caveat against the issue of a warrant to arrest the property filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 5;
-- src:4327 | ( b )
-- src:4328 | a caveat against the issue of a release and payment out of Court filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 14.
-- src:4329 | (3) Where a document to which paragraph (2) applies is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service and is subsequently accepted by the Registrar, it is deemed to be filed, served, delivered or conveyed — ( a )
-- src:4330 | where the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed by electronic transmission, on the date and at the time that the Registrar accepts the document, as reflected in the computer system of the Registrar; or
-- src:4331 | ( b )
-- src:4332 | where the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed via a service bureau, on the date and at the time that the Registrar accepts the document, as reflected in the computer system of the Registrar.
-- src:4333 | (4) Where an originating process is filed or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service and it is subsequently accepted by the Registrar, it is deemed to be issued — ( a )
-- src:4334 | where the document is filed or conveyed by electronic transmission, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider in the computer system of the electronic filing service provider; and
-- src:4335 | ( b )
-- src:4336 | where the document is filed or conveyed via a service bureau, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the Registrar in the computer system of the Registrar.
-- src:4337 | (5) The registered user may produce a record of the transmission issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau (as the case may be) together with a copy of the notification of acceptance of the document by the Registrar as evidence of — ( a )
-- src:4338 | the filing or issuance of an originating process;
-- src:4339 | ( b )
-- src:4340 | the filing, service, delivery or conveyance of any other document; or
-- src:4341 | ( c )
-- src:4342 | the date and time either or both of these events took place.
-- src:4343 | (6) If the Registrar is satisfied for any reason that a document should be treated as having been filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar, or issued, at some earlier date and time, than the date and time provided for under paragraph (1), (3) or (4), the Registrar may cause the electronic filing service to reflect such earlier date and time, and that earlier date and time is deemed for all purposes to be the date and time on and at which the document was filed, served, delivered, conveyed or issued, as the case may be.
@ref O 28 r 10 the moment the document is deemed filed (src:4319-4343)
GIVEN how IS A `o 28 r 10(1) how the document reached the Registrar`
      `the document is one to which paragraph (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved by the provider in the provider's computer system` IS A Moment
      `the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved by the Registrar in the Registrar's computer system` IS A Moment
      `the moment the Registrar accepts it as reflected in the Registrar's computer system` IS A Moment
      `the earlier moment the Registrar has caused the electronic filing service to reflect` IS A MAYBE Moment
GIVETH A Moment
`o 28 r 10 the moment the document is deemed filed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier moment the Registrar has caused the electronic filing service to reflect`
    WHEN JUST earlier THEN earlier
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the document is one to which paragraph (2) applies`
        THEN `the moment the Registrar accepts it as reflected in the Registrar's computer system`
        ELSE CONSIDER how
             WHEN `o 28 r 10(1)(c) via a service bureau` THEN `the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved by the Registrar in the Registrar's computer system`
             OTHERWISE `the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved by the provider in the provider's computer system`

-- src:4329 | (3) Where a document to which paragraph (2) applies is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service and is subsequently accepted by the Registrar, it is deemed to be filed, served, delivered or conveyed — ( a )
-- src:4330 | where the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed by electronic transmission, on the date and at the time that the Registrar accepts the document, as reflected in the computer system of the Registrar; or
-- src:4331 | ( b )
-- src:4332 | where the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed via a service bureau, on the date and at the time that the Registrar accepts the document, as reflected in the computer system of the Registrar.
@ref O 28 r 10(3) (src:4329-4332)
GIVEN `the document is a caveat to which paragraph (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is filed with, served on, delivered or conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar subsequently accepts it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 10(3) the caveat is deemed filed at the moment the Registrar accepts it` MEANS
    IF `the document is a caveat to which paragraph (2) applies` AND `it is filed with, served on, delivered or conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service` AND `the Registrar subsequently accepts it`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is deemed to be filed, served, delivered or conveyed — on the date and at the time that the Registrar accepts the document, as reflected in the computer system of the Registrar"
-- src:4333 | (4) Where an originating process is filed or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service and it is subsequently accepted by the Registrar, it is deemed to be issued — ( a )
-- src:4334 | where the document is filed or conveyed by electronic transmission, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider in the computer system of the electronic filing service provider; and
-- src:4335 | ( b )
-- src:4336 | where the document is filed or conveyed via a service bureau, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the Registrar in the computer system of the Registrar.
@ref O 28 r 10(4) (src:4333-4336)
GIVEN `the originating process is filed or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar subsequently accepts it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 10(4) the originating process is deemed issued` MEANS
    IF `the originating process is filed or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service` AND `the Registrar subsequently accepts it`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an originating process is filed or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service and it is subsequently accepted by the Registrar, it is deemed to be issued"

-- The moment an originating process is deemed issued (r 10(4)): (a) by transmission: retrievable in the provider's
-- system; (b) via a service bureau: retrievable in the Registrar's system.
@ref O 28 r 10(4) the moment (src:4333-4336)
GIVEN `it is filed or conveyed via a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved by the provider in the provider's computer system` IS A Moment
      `the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved by the Registrar in the Registrar's computer system` IS A Moment
GIVETH A Moment
`o 28 r 10(4) the moment the originating process is deemed issued` MEANS
    IF `it is filed or conveyed via a service bureau`
    THEN `the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved by the Registrar in the Registrar's computer system`
    ELSE `the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved by the provider in the provider's computer system`

-- src:4337 | (5) The registered user may produce a record of the transmission issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau (as the case may be) together with a copy of the notification of acceptance of the document by the Registrar as evidence of — ( a )
-- src:4338 | the filing or issuance of an originating process;
-- src:4339 | ( b )
-- src:4340 | the filing, service, delivery or conveyance of any other document; or
-- src:4341 | ( c )
-- src:4342 | the date and time either or both of these events took place.
@ref O 28 r 10(5) (src:4337-4342)
GIVEN `the record of the transmission is issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is produced together with a copy of the Registrar's notification of acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 10(5) the registered user may produce a record as evidence of filing or issuance` MEANS
    IF `the record of the transmission is issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau` AND `it is produced together with a copy of the Registrar's notification of acceptance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registered user may produce a record of the transmission issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau (as the case may be) together with a copy of the notification of acceptance of the document by the Registrar as evidence of"
-- src:4343 | (6) If the Registrar is satisfied for any reason that a document should be treated as having been filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar, or issued, at some earlier date and time, than the date and time provided for under paragraph (1), (3) or (4), the Registrar may cause the electronic filing service to reflect such earlier date and time, and that earlier date and time is deemed for all purposes to be the date and time on and at which the document was filed, served, delivered, conveyed or issued, as the case may be.
@ref O 28 r 10(6) (src:4343)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied for any reason that the document should be treated as filed or issued at an earlier date and time than paragraph (1), (3) or (4) provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 10(6) the Registrar may cause an earlier date and time to be reflected` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied for any reason that the document should be treated as filed or issued at an earlier date and time than paragraph (1), (3) or (4) provides`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Registrar is satisfied for any reason that a document should be treated as having been filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar, or issued, at some earlier date and time, than the date and time provided for under paragraph (1), (3) or (4), the Registrar may cause the electronic filing service to reflect such earlier date and time"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 11 -- when time for service begins to run (seam S-F2)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "Only begins to run from": the bar of the ruling of 2026-11-05 (d) is encoded as its own function, and the
-- positive statement ("begins to run from the time ... is received") as another.
-- src:4345 | 11. —(1) Where a document is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar by electronic transmission, the time for service of that document only begins to run from the time that the Registrar’s notification of his or her acceptance of the document is received in the computer system of that registered user. (2) Where a document is filed with or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar via a service bureau, the time for service of that document only begins to run from the time that the Registrar’s notification of his or her acceptance of the document is received by the service bureau.
@ref O 28 r 11(1) and (2) (src:4345)
GIVEN `the Registrar's notification of acceptance has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 11(1) time for service cannot yet begin to run` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar's notification of acceptance has been received`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the time for service of that document only begins to run from the time that the Registrar’s notification of his or her acceptance of the document is received"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref O 28 r 11(1) and (2) (src:4345)
GIVEN `the Registrar's notification of acceptance has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 11(1) time for service has begun to run` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar's notification of acceptance has been received`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the time for service of that document only begins to run from the time that the Registrar’s notification of his or her acceptance of the document is received"

-- r 11(3): a notification received on a day that is not a working day is deemed received on the next working day.
-- The next working day is found by looking at one day after another (at most 14, which is more than any run of
-- non-working days); `o 1 r 3(1) a day is a working day` is the keel's function.
-- src:4346 | (3) If the Registrar’s notification referred to in paragraphs (1) and (2) is received in the computer system or the service bureau respectively on a day other than a working day, it is deemed for the purpose of this Rule to have been received on the next working day.
@ref O 28 r 11(3) (src:4346)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Court calendar`
      fuel IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`o 28 r 11(3) the first working day on or after` MEANS
    IF fuel AT MOST 0
    THEN day
    ELSE CONSIDER `o 1 r 3(1) a day is a working day` day calendar
         WHEN JUST isWorking THEN
             IF isWorking
             THEN day
             ELSE `o 28 r 11(3) the first working day on or after` (day PLUS 1) calendar (fuel MINUS 1)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN day

-- src:4345 | 11. —(1) Where a document is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar by electronic transmission, the time for service of that document only begins to run from the time that the Registrar’s notification of his or her acceptance of the document is received in the computer system of that registered user. (2) Where a document is filed with or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar via a service bureau, the time for service of that document only begins to run from the time that the Registrar’s notification of his or her acceptance of the document is received by the service bureau.
-- src:4346 | (3) If the Registrar’s notification referred to in paragraphs (1) and (2) is received in the computer system or the service bureau respectively on a day other than a working day, it is deemed for the purpose of this Rule to have been received on the next working day.
@ref O 28 r 11 the moment time for service begins to run (src:4345-4346)
GIVEN way IS A `o 28 r 10(1) how the document reached the Registrar`
      `the moment the notification is received in the registered user's computer system` IS A Moment
      `the moment the notification is received by the service bureau` IS A Moment
      calendar IS A `Court calendar`
GIVETH A Moment
`o 28 r 11 the moment time for service begins to run` MEANS
    LET received MEANS
            CONSIDER way
            WHEN `o 28 r 10(1)(c) via a service bureau` THEN `the moment the notification is received by the service bureau`
            OTHERWISE `the moment the notification is received in the registered user's computer system`
    IN  CONSIDER `o 1 r 3(1) a day is a working day` (received's `day of the moment`) calendar
        WHEN JUST isWorking THEN
            IF isWorking
            THEN received
            ELSE Moment WITH
                     `day of the moment` IS `o 28 r 11(3) the first working day on or after` ((received's `day of the moment`) PLUS 1) calendar 14
                     `minutes after midnight` IS 0
        WHEN NOTHING THEN received

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 12 -- service of documents (seam S-S2)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4348 | 12. —(1) If a document — ( a )
-- src:4349 | other than a document which is required by these Rules to be served personally; or
-- src:4350 | ( b )
-- src:4351 | being a document which is required by these Rules to be served personally and which the party to be served has agreed may be served using the electronic filing service,
-- src:4352 | is required under any other provision of these Rules to be served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by a person to any other person and that person is an authorised user or a registered user or is represented by a solicitor who is an authorised user or a registered user (called in this Rule the person on whom the document is served), such service, delivery or conveyance may be effected by using the electronic filing service by electronic transmission or via a service bureau.
@ref O 28 r 12(1) (src:4348-4352)
GIVEN `the document is required by these Rules to be served personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party to be served has agreed that it may be served using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to be served is an authorised user or a registered user, or is represented by a solicitor who is` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(1) service may be effected using the electronic filing service` MEANS
    IF ((NOT `the document is required by these Rules to be served personally`) OR `the party to be served has agreed that it may be served using the electronic filing service`)
       AND `the person to be served is an authorised user or a registered user, or is represented by a solicitor who is`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a document — other than a document which is required by these Rules to be served personally; or being a document which is required by these Rules to be served personally and which the party to be served has agreed may be served using the electronic filing service — is required under any other provision of these Rules to be served ... and that person is an authorised user or a registered user or is represented by a solicitor who is an authorised user or a registered user ... such service ... may be effected": the "If" is not met

-- src:4353 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)( b ), a party who has instructed the party’s solicitor to accept service of a document which is required by these Rules to be served personally is deemed to have agreed to be served using the electronic filing service.
@ref O 28 r 12(2) (src:4353)
GIVEN `the party has instructed the party's solicitor to accept service of a document which is required by these Rules to be served personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(2) the party is deemed to have agreed to be served using the electronic filing service` MEANS
    IF `the party has instructed the party's solicitor to accept service of a document which is required by these Rules to be served personally`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a party who has instructed the party's solicitor to accept service of a document which is required by these Rules to be served personally is deemed to have agreed to be served using the electronic filing service"

-- The moment (S-F2's sibling S-S2): in both limbs of r 12(3) it is the moment the document becomes capable of being
-- retrieved by the provider in the provider's computer system.
-- src:4354 | (3) The document is deemed to be served, delivered or otherwise conveyed — ( a )
-- src:4355 | where the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by electronic transmission from the computer system of the authorised user or registered user, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider in the computer system of the electronic filing service provider; and
-- src:4356 | ( b )
-- src:4357 | where the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider in the computer system of the electronic filing service provider.
@ref O 28 r 12(3) (src:4354-4357)
GIVEN `the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved by the provider in the provider's computer system` IS A Moment
GIVETH A Moment
`o 28 r 12 the moment service is deemed effected` MEANS
    `the moment it becomes capable of being retrieved by the provider in the provider's computer system`

-- src:4354 | (3) The document is deemed to be served, delivered or otherwise conveyed — ( a )
-- src:4355 | where the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by electronic transmission from the computer system of the authorised user or registered user, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider in the computer system of the electronic filing service provider; and
@ref O 28 r 12(3)(a) (src:4354-4355)
GIVEN `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by electronic transmission from the computer system of the authorised user or registered user` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(3)(a) the document is deemed served by electronic transmission` MEANS
    IF `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by electronic transmission from the computer system of the authorised user or registered user`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The document is deemed to be served, delivered or otherwise conveyed — where the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by electronic transmission from the computer system of the authorised user or registered user, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider"
-- src:4356 | ( b )
-- src:4357 | where the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider in the computer system of the electronic filing service provider.
@ref O 28 r 12(3)(b) (src:4356-4357)
GIVEN `the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(3)(b) the remotely composed document is deemed served` MEANS
    IF `the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider, on the date and at the time that the document becomes capable of being retrieved by the electronic filing service provider"
-- src:4358 | (4) The person serving the document may produce a record of the service, delivery or conveyance to the person on whom the document is served which is issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau as evidence of the service, delivery or conveyance, as well as the date and time of such service, delivery or conveyance.
@ref O 28 r 12(4) (src:4358)
GIVEN `the record is issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(4) the person serving may produce a record of service as evidence` MEANS
    IF `the record is issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The person serving the document may produce a record of the service, delivery or conveyance to the person on whom the document is served which is issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau (as the case may be) as evidence of the service, delivery or conveyance, as well as the date and time"
-- src:4359 | (5) The person serving the document may file a Registrar’s certificate of service issued through the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau in lieu of an affidavit of service and the certificate is regarded as prima facie evidence of such service, delivery or conveyance on the date and at the time as stated.
@ref O 28 r 12(5) lieu (src:4359)
GIVEN `the certificate is a Registrar's certificate of service issued through the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(5) the person serving may file a Registrar's certificate of service in lieu of an affidavit` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is a Registrar's certificate of service issued through the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The person serving the document may file a Registrar’s certificate of service issued through the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau (as the case may be) in lieu of an affidavit of service"
-- src:4359 | (5) The person serving the document may file a Registrar’s certificate of service issued through the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau in lieu of an affidavit of service and the certificate is regarded as prima facie evidence of such service, delivery or conveyance on the date and at the time as stated.
@ref O 28 r 12(5) prima facie (src:4359)
GIVEN `the person serving files a Registrar's certificate of service in lieu of an affidavit of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(5) the certificate is regarded as prima facie evidence of service` MEANS
    IF `the person serving files a Registrar's certificate of service in lieu of an affidavit of service`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the certificate is regarded as prima facie evidence of such service, delivery or conveyance on the date and at the time as stated"
-- src:4360 | (6) Where a document has to be served, delivered or conveyed by the person serving the document to more than one person, the person serving may effect such service, delivery or conveyance using the electronic filing service on such of those persons who are registered users or authorised users, and paragraphs (1), (3), (4) and (5) apply with such modifications as are necessary.
@ref O 28 r 12(6) (src:4360)
GIVEN `the document has to be served, delivered or conveyed on more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a registered user or an authorised user` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(6) service on more than one person may be effected using the electronic filing service on those who are users` MEANS
    IF `the document has to be served, delivered or conveyed on more than one person`
    THEN IF `the person is a registered user or an authorised user`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a document has to be served, delivered or conveyed by the person serving the document to more than one person, the person serving may effect such service, delivery or conveyance using the electronic filing service on such of those persons who are registered users or authorised users"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a document has to be served, delivered or conveyed by the person serving the document to more than one person, the person serving may effect such service, delivery or conveyance using the electronic filing service on such of those persons who are registered users or authorised users"
-- src:4361 | (7) Any document which is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by a registered user to a person through the electronic filing service using an identification code is deemed to have been so served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by the registered user and with his or her intention to do so.
@ref O 28 r 12(7) (src:4361)
GIVEN `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by a registered user to a person through the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(7) the document is deemed served by the registered user with that user's intention` MEANS
    IF `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by a registered user to a person through the electronic filing service` AND `it is done using an identification code`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any document which is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by a registered user to a person through the electronic filing service using an identification code is deemed to have been so served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by the registered user and with his or her intention to do so"
-- src:4362 | (8) Any document which is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by an authorised user (other than an employee of a service bureau) to a person through the electronic filing service using an identification code is deemed to have been so served, delivered or otherwise conveyed — ( a )
-- src:4363 | by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the registered user to whom the authorised user belongs; and
@ref O 28 r 12(8)(a) (src:4362-4363)
GIVEN `the document is served through the electronic filing service by an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(8)(a) the document is deemed served by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the registered user` MEANS
    IF `the document is served through the electronic filing service by an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau` AND `it is done using an identification code`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the registered user to whom the authorised user belongs" (open convention question QE)
-- src:4364 | ( b )
-- src:4365 | with the intention of that registered user to do so.
@ref O 28 r 12(8)(b) (src:4364-4365)
GIVEN `the document is served through the electronic filing service by an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(8)(b) the document is deemed served with the intention of the registered user` MEANS
    IF `the document is served through the electronic filing service by an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau` AND `it is done using an identification code`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the intention of that registered user to do so" (open convention question QE)
-- src:4366 | (9) Any document which is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau, is deemed to have been so served, delivered or otherwise conveyed — ( a )
-- src:4367 | on behalf and with the authority of the person tendering the document to the service bureau for such purpose and with the intention of that person to do so; or
@ref O 28 r 12(9)(a) (src:4366-4367)
GIVEN `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(9)(a) the document is deemed served on behalf and with the authority of the person tendering it` MEANS
    IF `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau`
    THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on behalf and with the authority of the person tendering the document to the service bureau for such purpose and with the intention of that person to do so"
-- src:4368 | ( b )
-- src:4369 | where the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for the person’s principal, on behalf and with the authority of the person’s principal and with the intention of the principal to do so.
@ref O 28 r 12(9)(b) (src:4368-4369)
GIVEN `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for a principal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 12(9)(b) the document is deemed served on behalf and with the authority of the principal` MEANS
    IF `the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for a principal`
    THEN IF `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by an authorised user who is an employee of a service bureau`
         THEN `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for the person’s principal, on behalf and with the authority of the person’s principal and with the intention of the principal to do so"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the person tendering the document to the service bureau is acting as agent for the person’s principal, on behalf and with the authority of the person’s principal and with the intention of the principal to do so"
-- src:4370 | (10) To avoid doubt, it is declared that any document which is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed to a person using an identification code in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service is a secure electronic record within the meaning of the Electronic Transactions Act.
@ref O 28 r 12(10) (src:4370)
