    IF `the practice directions issued by the Registrar prescribe a manner` AND `the amendment is effected in that manner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "Amendments to documents must be effected in the manner prescribed in any practice directions for the time being issued by the Registrar" (a bare must not done; open convention question QB)
-- src:4377 | 15. —(1) Affidavits which are filed in Court using the electronic filing service may be used in all proceedings to the same extent and for the same purposes as paper affidavits filed in Court. (2) Where an affidavit is to be filed in Court using the electronic filing service, it must comply with the following requirements: ( a )
