-- r 15(2)(c): the original is retained for 7 years after it is filed.  The last day of the 7 years is counted under Order 3,
-- Rule 3 (an input).  Retained to the end of it: JUST TRUE.  Given up before: JUST FALSE (the text fixes the period).
-- Still held, and the 7 years have not ended: NOTHING.  Still held after they ended: JUST TRUE.
-- src:4381 | ( c )
-- src:4382 | the original paper affidavit must be retained by the party who filed it for a period of 7 years after it is filed.
@ref O 28 r 15(2)(c) (src:4381-4382)
GIVEN `the date the party ceased to retain the original` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day of the 7 years` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 15(2)(c) the original paper affidavit is retained for 7 years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the party ceased to retain the original`
    WHEN JUST ceased THEN
        IF ceased GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day of the 7 years`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the text fixes the period in its own words ("for a period of 7 years after it is filed"), and the original was given up within it
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date asked about` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day of the 7 years`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 7 years have not yet ended and the original is still held

-- 7 years, in months: the core's `Time unit` has no years (recorded in NEEDS-CORE.md).
@ref O 28 r 15(2)(c) 7 years (src:4381-4382)
`o 28 r 15(2)(c) the period of retention in months` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 84
    `period unit` IS Months
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:4383 | (3) Despite paragraph (2)( c ), if the original paper affidavit subsequently becomes unavailable within 7 years after it was filed, the Court may grant permission for the electronic image of the original paper affidavit filed in Court using the electronic filing service to be used in the proceedings for which it was filed, or in any other proceedings.
@ref O 28 r 15(3) (src:4383)
GIVEN `the original paper affidavit became unavailable within 7 years after it was filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 15(3) the Court may permit the electronic image to be used` MEANS
    IF `the original paper affidavit became unavailable within 7 years after it was filed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the original paper affidavit subsequently becomes unavailable within 7 years after it was filed, the Court may grant permission for the electronic image of the original paper affidavit filed in Court using the electronic filing service to be used in the proceedings for which it was filed, or in any other proceedings"

-- r 16: which information prevails where the electronic template and the document disagree.
-- src:4385 | 16. Where a document was filed using the electronic filing service, and there is any inconsistency between — ( a )
-- src:4386 | the information entered into the electronic template of the document or of the transmission containing the document; and
-- src:4387 | ( b )
-- src:4388 | the information contained in the document,
-- src:4389 | the information contained in the document prevails where that document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider, and in all other cases the information entered into the electronic template of the document prevails.
@ref O 28 r 16 (src:4385-4389)
GIVEN `the document was filed using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an inconsistency between the information entered into the electronic template and the information contained in the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 16 the information contained in the document prevails` MEANS
    IF `the document was filed using the electronic filing service` AND `there is an inconsistency between the information entered into the electronic template and the information contained in the document`
    THEN JUST `the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider` -- the text says the template prevails "in all other cases"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a document was filed using the electronic filing service, and there is any inconsistency between"

@ref O 28 r 16 template (src:4385-4389)
GIVEN `the document was filed using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an inconsistency between the information entered into the electronic template and the information contained in the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 28 r 16 the information entered into the electronic template prevails` MEANS
    IF `the document was filed using the electronic filing service` AND `there is an inconsistency between the information entered into the electronic template and the information contained in the document`
    THEN JUST (NOT `the document is remotely composed on the computer system of the electronic filing service provider`) -- "in all other cases the information entered into the electronic template of the document prevails"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a document was filed using the electronic filing service, and there is any inconsistency between"

